IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Age Discrimination Act 2004 (Cth) -- what an older worker meets.
--
-- SEAT: the older worker -- the employee or job applicant to whom the Act is applied. "Can I be made to retire at an age?
-- Was I discriminated against because of my age? Is there an exemption that lets them do it? Where do I complain?" Every
-- question below is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Direct and indirect discrimination on the ground of age (ss 14, 15, 16; s 6 disability excluded;
-- s 5 "age" includes age group, "employment" includes part-time, temporary and contract-for-services work); the Act's
-- reach as an input (s 10); discrimination in employment (s 18(1), (2)) with the domestic duties and inherent
-- requirements exemptions (s 18(3)-(5)); youth wages (s 25); requests for information (s 32); positive discrimination
-- (s 33); religious bodies (s 35); direct compliance with superannuation, other laws, court orders, minimum wage orders
-- and fair work instruments, and taxation laws (ss 38, 39, 40); Commission exemptions (ss 44, 47); victimisation (ss
-- 47A, 51); advertisements (s 50); the bar on a federal complaint after a State complaint (s 12(4)). From the Australian
-- Human Rights Commission Act 1986: "unlawful discrimination" (s 3(1)), lodging a complaint (s 46P), termination for
-- lateness (s 46PH(1)(b)) and the 60 days to go to court (s 46PO(2)).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 57, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025; register id
-- C2026C00266), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01302.txt.
-- Also used: Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986, Compilation No. 58, compilation date 18 September 2026
-- (includes amendments up to Act No. 87, 2026; register id C2026C00416), as deposited at
-- ../../../australian-human-rights-commission-act-1986/registers/source-bundle/C2004A03366.txt -- ss 3(1), 46P, 46PH,
-- 46PO only. No regulations set a number this encoding needs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The other areas of Part 4 (commission agents, contract workers, partnerships, qualifying bodies,
-- registered organisations, employment agencies, education, premises, goods and services, accommodation, land,
-- Commonwealth laws and programs: ss 19-24, 26-31); the exemptions the older worker's events do not need (s 34
-- charities, s 36 voluntary bodies, s 37 actuarial data, s 41 pensions, s 41A Commonwealth employment programs, s 42
-- health, s 43 migration); Schedules 1 and 2 (which Acts are covered by s 39(1), (1A) is an input); the constitutional
-- heads in s 10 (an input); remedies the court may order; the President's inquiry and conciliation; penalty unit
-- values (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not deposited); the Commission and the Age Discrimination Commissioner as institutions
-- (machinery); the Fair Work Act 2009 general protections (ss 351, 772), which give a parallel route and are out of
-- scope in the Fair Work Act baseline too.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- Judgments the Act hands to a court or the President are INPUTS ("if a court would find that ..."). See NOTES.md.

§ `Age Discrimination Act 2004 -- the older worker's questions`

§§ `ss 6, 14, 15, 16 -- was I discriminated against on the ground of my age`

-- s 14: a person "discriminates against another person (the aggrieved person) on the ground of the age of the aggrieved
-- person if: (a) the discriminator treats or proposes to treat the aggrieved person less favourably than, in
-- circumstances that are the same or are not materially different, the discriminator treats or would treat a person of
-- a different age; and (b) the discriminator does so because of: (i) the age of the aggrieved person; or (ii) a
-- characteristic that appertains generally to persons of the age of the aggrieved person; or (iii) a characteristic
-- that is generally imputed to persons of the age of the aggrieved person."
-- s 16: where an act is done for 2 or more reasons and one of them "(whether or not it is the dominant or a substantial
-- reason)" is age or such a characteristic, the act "is taken to be done because of the age of the person".
-- s 6: age discrimination "is taken not to include ... discrimination ... on the ground of a disability of the person".
-- s 15(1): indirect discrimination if "(a) the discriminator imposes, or proposes to impose, a condition, requirement or
-- practice; and (b) the condition, requirement or practice is not reasonable in the circumstances; and (c) the
-- condition, requirement or practice has, or is likely to have, the effect of disadvantaging persons of the same age as
-- the aggrieved person." (2): "the burden of proving that the condition, requirement or practice is reasonable in the
-- circumstances lies on the discriminator."
-- Plain gloss: direct discrimination is being treated worse because of your age (or what people assume about people your
-- age); indirect discrimination is a rule that looks neutral but disadvantages people your age and that the employer
-- cannot show is reasonable.
DECLARE `How I was treated` HAS
    `I was treated less favourably than a person of a different age would be` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you were treated, or are to be treated, less favourably than someone of a different age would be in circumstances that are the same or not materially different
    `my age was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether your age (or age group) was a reason for it, even if not the main reason (s 16)
    `a characteristic of people my age was one of the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a characteristic that people your age generally have, or are generally assumed to have, was a reason for it
    `that characteristic is a disability of mine` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether that characteristic is in truth a disability of yours (s 6: then it is a disability question, not an age question)
    `a condition, requirement or practice was imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a condition, requirement or practice was imposed, or is proposed, on you
    `it disadvantages people my age` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it has, or is likely to have, the effect of disadvantaging people of your age
    `the employer has shown it is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the employer (who bears the burden, s 15(2)) has shown the condition, requirement or practice is reasonable in the circumstances

DECLARE `Kind of age discrimination` IS ONE OF
    `direct discrimination (s 14)`
    `indirect discrimination (s 15)`
    `not discrimination on the ground of my age`

-- s 6 is read as taking a disability out of the "characteristic" limbs only; where age itself is a reason, s 16 still
-- makes it age discrimination (an inference).
@export How, if at all, was I discriminated against on the ground of my age (ss 6, 14, 15, 16)?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `How I was treated` @desc What was done to you and why
GIVETH A `Kind of age discrimination`
DECIDE `How was I discriminated against` IS
    BRANCH
      IF     `the treatment`'s `I was treated less favourably than a person of a different age would be`
         AND (   `the treatment`'s `my age was one of the reasons`
              OR (    `the treatment`'s `a characteristic of people my age was one of the reasons`
                  AND (NOT `the treatment`'s `that characteristic is a disability of mine`)))
        THEN `direct discrimination (s 14)`
      IF     `the treatment`'s `a condition, requirement or practice was imposed on me`
         AND (NOT `the treatment`'s `the employer has shown it is reasonable`)
         AND `the treatment`'s `it disadvantages people my age`
        THEN `indirect discrimination (s 15)`
      OTHERWISE `not discrimination on the ground of my age`

@export Was I discriminated against on the ground of my age (ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `How I was treated` @desc What was done to you and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I discriminated against on the ground of my age` IF
    NOT (`How was I discriminated against` `the treatment` EQUALS `not discrimination on the ground of my age`)

§§ `s 18 -- discrimination in employment, with ss 25, 33, 35, 38-40, 47`

-- s 18(1): "It is unlawful for an employer ... to discriminate against a person on the ground of the other person's age:
-- (a) in the arrangements made for the purpose of determining who should be offered employment; or (b) in determining
-- who should be offered employment; or (c) in the terms or conditions on which employment is offered."
-- s 18(2): "... to discriminate against an employee on the ground of the employee's age: (a) in the terms or conditions
-- of employment that the employer affords the employee; or (b) by denying the employee access, or limiting the
-- employee's access, to opportunities for promotion, transfer or training, or to any other benefits associated with
-- employment; or (c) by dismissing the employee; or (d) by subjecting the employee to any other detriment."
-- s 5: "employment includes: (a) part-time and temporary employment; and (b) work under a contract for services ..."
DECLARE `What was done at work` IS ONE OF
    `in the arrangements for deciding who is offered employment`
    `in deciding who is offered employment`
    `in the terms or conditions on which employment is offered`
    `in the terms or conditions of my employment`
    `by denying or limiting my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
    `by dismissing me`
    `by subjecting me to any other detriment`

-- s 33: Part 4 "does not make it unlawful ... by an act that is consistent with the purposes of this Act, if: (a) the act
-- provides a bona fide benefit to persons of a particular age; or (b) the act is intended to meet a need that arises out
-- of the age of persons of a particular age; or (c) the act is intended to reduce a disadvantage experienced by people of
-- a particular age." Its own example under (c): "additional notice entitlements for older workers".
DECLARE `Positive purpose` IS ONE OF
    `no positive purpose`
    `a bona fide benefit to people of a particular age`
    `meeting a need arising from the age of people of a particular age`
    `reducing a disadvantage experienced by people of a particular age`

-- ss 38-40: Part 4 "does not make unlawful anything done by a person in direct compliance with" -- s 38: a Commonwealth
-- superannuation Act or instrument; s 39(1), (1A): an Act, instrument or provision covered by Schedule 1 or 2; s 39(4),
-- (5): a State or Territory Act or instrument not specified in the regulations; s 39(7): "an order of a court"; s
-- 39(8): "(a) an order, determination or award of a court or tribunal having power to fix minimum wages; (b) ... a fair
-- work instrument (within the meaning of the Fair Work Act 2009)"; s 40: "a taxation law". The s 39(8) note: a person
-- does not comply with a provision of an industrial instrument "that has no effect". The s 39(2) two-year period for
-- other Commonwealth laws ended two years after commencement in 2004 and is not encoded.
DECLARE `What the employer was directly complying with` IS ONE OF
    `nothing that exempts it`
    `a Commonwealth superannuation law (s 38)`
    `an Act or instrument covered by Schedule 1 or 2 (s 39(1), (1A))`
    `a State or Territory law not specified in the regulations (s 39(4))`
    `a court order (s 39(7))`
    `a minimum wage order or a fair work instrument that has effect (s 39(8))`
    `a taxation law (s 40)`

DECLARE `My work case` HAS
    `the Act reaches it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Act reaches the discrimination under s 10 -- for example the employer is a trading or financial corporation, the Commonwealth, or it falls within the ILO Discrimination (Employment and Occupation) Convention (s 10(7))
    `the treatment` IS A `How I was treated`
    @desc What was done to you and why
    `what was done` IS A `What was done at work`
    @desc Where in employment it happened (s 18)
    `it is a job doing domestic duties where the employer lives` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the job is to perform domestic duties on the premises where the employer lives (s 18(3))
    `a court would find I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a court would find you unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the particular job because of your age, taking into account your training, qualifications, experience, your performance if already employed, and other relevant factors (s 18(4), (5))
    `how old I am` IS A NUMBER
    @desc Your age in years
    `it is about youth wages` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it concerns youth wages -- pay for people under 21 -- in offering work or paying for it (s 25)
    `its positive purpose` IS A `Positive purpose`
    @desc Whether it is meant to benefit, meet a need of, or reduce a disadvantage of people of a particular age (s 33)
    `it is consistent with the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the act is consistent with the purposes of the Act (s 33)
    `the employer is a religious body following its doctrines` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the employer is a body established for religious purposes and the act conforms to its doctrines, tenets or beliefs or is necessary to avoid injury to adherents' religious sensitivities (s 35)
    `the employer was directly complying with` IS A `What the employer was directly complying with`
    @desc Any law, order or instrument the employer was directly complying with (ss 38-40)
    `the employer acted under a Commission exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the employer acted in accordance with an exemption the Australian Human Rights Commission granted under s 44 (s 47)

DECLARE `What the Act says about it` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`
    `not discrimination on the ground of my age (ss 14-16)`
    `outside the reach of the Act (s 10)`
    `not unlawful: a domestic job in the employer's home (s 18(3))`
    `not unlawful: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
    `not unlawful: youth wages (s 25)`
    `not unlawful: positive discrimination (s 33)`
    `not unlawful: a religious body's practice (s 35)`
    `not unlawful: direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
    `not unlawful: a Commission exemption (s 47)`

-- s 18(3): "Paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not make it unlawful ... in connection with employment to perform domestic duties
-- on the premises on which the first-mentioned person resides."
GIVEN `the area` IS A `What was done at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the area is about who is offered the job` IF
    CONSIDER `the area`
    WHEN `in the arrangements for deciding who is offered employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `in deciding who is offered employment` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 18(4): "Paragraphs (1)(a), (1)(b) and (2)(c) do not make it unlawful for an employer to discriminate ... if the other
-- person is unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the particular employment because of his or her age."
-- So the inherent requirements exemption does NOT cover the terms of an offer, the terms of employment, access to
-- promotion or training, or other detriment.
GIVEN `the area` IS A `What was done at work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the inherent requirements exemption can apply to it` IF
        `the area is about who is offered the job` `the area`
    OR  `the area` EQUALS `by dismissing me`

-- s 25(1): Division 2 does not make unlawful discrimination "in relation to youth wages: (a) in the arrangements made for
-- the purpose of determining who should be offered work; or (b) in determining who should be offered work; or (c) in
-- payment, or offer of payment, of remuneration for work." (2): "youth wages means remuneration for persons who are under
-- 21." Payment is read as falling within the terms or conditions areas of s 18 (an inference).
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My work case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the youth wages exemption applies` IF
        `the case`'s `it is about youth wages`
    AND `the case`'s `how old I am` LESS THAN 21
    AND (   `the area is about who is offered the job` (`the case`'s `what was done`)
         OR `the case`'s `what was done` EQUALS `in the terms or conditions on which employment is offered`
         OR `the case`'s `what was done` EQUALS `in the terms or conditions of my employment`)

@export Is what was done to me at work unlawful age discrimination, or does an exemption cover it (s 18)?
GIVEN `the case` IS A `My work case` @desc What happened to you at work
GIVETH A `What the Act says about it`
DECIDE `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT `the case`'s `the Act reaches it`)
        THEN `outside the reach of the Act (s 10)`
      IF (NOT `Was I discriminated against on the ground of my age` (`the case`'s `the treatment`))
        THEN `not discrimination on the ground of my age (ss 14-16)`
      IF     `the case`'s `it is a job doing domestic duties where the employer lives`
         AND `the area is about who is offered the job` (`the case`'s `what was done`)
        THEN `not unlawful: a domestic job in the employer's home (s 18(3))`
      IF     `the case`'s `a court would find I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age`
         AND `the inherent requirements exemption can apply to it` (`the case`'s `what was done`)
        THEN `not unlawful: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
      IF `the youth wages exemption applies` `the case`
        THEN `not unlawful: youth wages (s 25)`
      IF     (NOT (`the case`'s `its positive purpose` EQUALS `no positive purpose`))
         AND `the case`'s `it is consistent with the purposes of the Act`
        THEN `not unlawful: positive discrimination (s 33)`
      IF `the case`'s `the employer is a religious body following its doctrines`
        THEN `not unlawful: a religious body's practice (s 35)`
      IF (NOT (`the case`'s `the employer was directly complying with` EQUALS `nothing that exempts it`))
        THEN `not unlawful: direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
      IF `the case`'s `the employer acted under a Commission exemption`
        THEN `not unlawful: a Commission exemption (s 47)`
      OTHERWISE `unlawful age discrimination in employment (s 18)`

§§ `s 18(2)(c) -- can I be made to retire at an age`

-- The Act sets no retirement age and contains no general exemption for one. Being made to retire because of reaching an
-- age is "dismissing the employee" on the ground of age, direct discrimination under s 14 (an inference from ss 14 and
-- 18(2)(c); the Act does not use the word "retirement" in s 18). Retiring by one's own choice involves no act of the
-- employer, so the Act has nothing to say about it.
DECLARE `My retirement` HAS
    `I am choosing to retire` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are retiring of your own choice rather than being required to
    `the Act reaches it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Act reaches your employer under s 10 (for example, a company that trades, or the Commonwealth)
    `a court would find I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a court would find you unable to carry out the inherent requirements of your job because of your age (s 18(4), (5))
    `the employer is a religious body following its doctrines` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the employer is a religious body acting in conformity with its doctrines or to avoid injury to adherents' religious sensitivities (s 35)
    `the employer was directly complying with` IS A `What the employer was directly complying with`
    @desc Any law, order or instrument requiring your retirement that the employer was directly complying with (ss 38-40)
    `the employer acted under a Commission exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a Commission exemption under s 44 covers it (s 47)

DECLARE `Whether I can be made to retire` IS ONE OF
    `no: making me retire because of my age is unlawful dismissal on the ground of age (s 18(2)(c))`
    `nobody is making me: retiring by choice is not discrimination`
    `not under this Act: it does not reach my employer (s 10)`
    `yes: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
    `yes: a religious body's practice (s 35)`
    `yes: in direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
    `yes: under a Commission exemption (s 47)`

`a forced retirement because of my age` MEANS `How I was treated` WITH
    `I was treated less favourably than a person of a different age would be` IS TRUE
    `my age was one of the reasons` IS TRUE
    `a characteristic of people my age was one of the reasons` IS FALSE
    `that characteristic is a disability of mine` IS FALSE
    `a condition, requirement or practice was imposed on me` IS FALSE
    `it disadvantages people my age` IS FALSE
    `the employer has shown it is reasonable` IS FALSE

@export Can I be made to retire because I have reached a certain age (ss 14, 18(2)(c), (4))?
GIVEN `my retirement` IS A `My retirement` @desc Your retirement and your employer
GIVETH A `Whether I can be made to retire`
DECIDE `Can I be made to retire at an age` IS
    IF `my retirement`'s `I am choosing to retire`
    THEN `nobody is making me: retiring by choice is not discrimination`
    ELSE CONSIDER `What does the Act say about what was done to me at work` `as a dismissal`
         WHEN `outside the reach of the Act (s 10)` THEN `not under this Act: it does not reach my employer (s 10)`
         WHEN `not unlawful: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
           THEN `yes: I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age (s 18(4))`
         WHEN `not unlawful: a religious body's practice (s 35)` THEN `yes: a religious body's practice (s 35)`
         WHEN `not unlawful: direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
           THEN `yes: in direct compliance with a law, order or instrument (ss 38-40)`
         WHEN `not unlawful: a Commission exemption (s 47)` THEN `yes: under a Commission exemption (s 47)`
         OTHERWISE `no: making me retire because of my age is unlawful dismissal on the ground of age (s 18(2)(c))`
    WHERE
      `as a dismissal` MEANS `My work case` WITH
          `the Act reaches it` IS `my retirement`'s `the Act reaches it`
          `the treatment` IS `a forced retirement because of my age`
          `what was done` IS `by dismissing me`
          `it is a job doing domestic duties where the employer lives` IS FALSE
          `a court would find I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age` IS `my retirement`'s `a court would find I cannot carry out the inherent requirements because of my age`
          `how old I am` IS 21
          `it is about youth wages` IS FALSE
          `its positive purpose` IS `no positive purpose`
          `it is consistent with the purposes of the Act` IS FALSE
          `the employer is a religious body following its doctrines` IS `my retirement`'s `the employer is a religious body following its doctrines`
          `the employer was directly complying with` IS `my retirement`'s `the employer was directly complying with`
          `the employer acted under a Commission exemption` IS `my retirement`'s `the employer acted under a Commission exemption`

§§ `s 32 -- may I be asked my age`

-- s 32: "It is unlawful for a person ... to request or require another person ... to provide information (whether by way
-- of completing a form or otherwise) if: (a) the information is requested or required in connection with, or for the
-- purposes of, the first person doing a particular act; and (b) under Division 2 or this Division, it would be unlawful
-- in particular circumstances for the first person, in doing that act, to discriminate against the other person on the
-- ground of the other person's age; and (c) persons of a different age would not be requested or required to provide the
-- information in circumstances that are the same or not materially different."
@export Is it unlawful for an employer to ask me for this information (s 32)?
GIVEN `it is asked for an act such as hiring or promoting me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is asked for in connection with, or for the purposes of, a particular act of the employer (for example deciding whether to hire you)
      `age discrimination in that act could be unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it would be unlawful in some circumstances for the employer, in doing that act, to discriminate against you because of your age
      `people of a different age would not be asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether people of a different age would not be asked for it in circumstances that are the same or not materially different
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it unlawful to ask me for this information` IF
        `it is asked for an act such as hiring or promoting me`
    AND `age discrimination in that act could be unlawful`
    AND `people of a different age would not be asked`

§§ `ss 47A, 51 -- am I protected from victimisation`

-- s 47A(2): victimisation by actual detriment if "(a) the first person engages in conduct; and (b) the first person's
-- conduct causes detriment to the second person; and (c) the first person intends that the first person's conduct cause
-- detriment to the second person; and (d) the detriment is caused without the consent of the second person; and (e) the
-- first person engages in the first person's conduct because the first person believes that" the second person has
-- complained, brought proceedings, given information, attended a conference, appeared as a witness, reasonably asserted
-- rights, or alleged an unlawful act -- or proposes to (ss 47A(2)(e)(i)-(vii)).
-- s 47A(3): by threat, if the first person threatens detriment, "(i) intends the second person to fear that the threat
-- will be carried out; or (ii) is reckless as to causing the second person to fear" it, and does so because of such a
-- belief. (5): "it is not necessary to prove that the person threatened actually feared that the threat would be
-- carried out."
DECLARE `What was done to me after I spoke up` HAS
    `conduct caused me detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether someone's conduct caused you detriment
    `they intended the detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether they intended their conduct to cause you detriment
    `I consented to the detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you consented to the detriment
    `they threatened me with detriment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether they threatened to cause detriment to you or to someone else (express or implied, conditional or not)
    `they meant me to fear it, or were reckless about it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether they intended you to fear the threat would be carried out, or were reckless about causing that fear
    `they did it because they believed I complained or asserted my rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether they acted because they believed you had made or proposed a complaint, proceedings, given information, attended a conference, been a witness, asserted rights under the Act, or alleged an unlawful act (s 47A(2)(e))

@export Am I being victimised for complaining or asserting my rights (s 47A)?
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to me after I spoke up` @desc What was done or threatened, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I being victimised` IF
        `what was done`'s `they did it because they believed I complained or asserted my rights`
    AND (   (    `what was done`'s `conduct caused me detriment`
             AND `what was done`'s `they intended the detriment`
             AND (NOT `what was done`'s `I consented to the detriment`))
         OR (    `what was done`'s `they threatened me with detriment`
             AND `what was done`'s `they meant me to fear it, or were reckless about it`))

-- s 51(1), (2): the same conduct is an offence. "Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months."
@export What is the longest a person who victimises me can be imprisoned, in months (s 51)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest a person who victimises me can be imprisoned in months` IS 6

§§ `s 50 -- is a job advertisement aimed at younger applicants an offence`

-- s 50(1): an offence to publish or display an advertisement or notice that "(c) ... indicates, or could reasonably be
-- understood as indicating, an intention to do an act; and (d) that act would be unlawful under Part 4. Penalty: 10
-- penalty units." (2): "Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(c)." The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes
-- Act 1914 s 4AA, not deposited: the answer is in penalty units.
@export Is a job advertisement that shuts out people my age an offence (s 50)?
GIVEN `it indicates an intention to do an act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the advertisement or notice indicates, or could reasonably be understood as indicating, an intention to do an act (for example to hire only people under 40)
      `that act would be unlawful under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether doing that act would be unlawful age discrimination (see s 18 and its exemptions)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the advertisement an offence` IF
        `it indicates an intention to do an act`
    AND `that act would be unlawful under Part 4`

@export What is the most the advertiser can be fined, in penalty units (s 50)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the advertiser can be fined in penalty units` IS 10

§§ `s 12(4) and AHRC Act ss 3, 46P, 46PH, 46PO -- can I complain to the Australian Human Rights Commission`

-- AHRC Act s 3(1): "unlawful discrimination means any acts, omissions or practices that are unlawful under: (aa) Part 4
-- of the Age Discrimination Act 2004 ... and includes any conduct that is an offence under: (ca) Division 2 of Part 5 of
-- the Age Discrimination Act 2004 (other than section 51 or 52)". So a s 50 advertisement can be complained of; s 51
-- victimisation as an offence cannot, but victimisation is itself unlawful under s 47A in Part 4.
-- AHRC Act s 46P(1): "A written complaint may be lodged with the Commission ... alleging that those acts, omissions or
-- practices are unlawful discrimination." (1A): "It must be reasonably arguable that the alleged acts, omissions or
-- practices are unlawful discrimination." (2): by "a person aggrieved", or "(c) by a person or trade union on behalf of
-- one or more other persons aggrieved". (4): the Commission "must take reasonable steps to provide appropriate
-- assistance" to put a complaint in writing.
-- ADA s 12(4): if a person "has made a complaint or initiated a proceeding under" a State or Territory discrimination law
-- about the act, "the person is not entitled to make a complaint or institute a proceeding under the Australian Human
-- Rights Commission Act 1986" alleging the act is unlawful under Part 4. (In Western Australia, the State law is the
-- Equal Opportunity Act 1984 -- named, not read here.)
DECLARE `My complaint` HAS
    `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the complaint is in writing (the Commission must help you put it in writing if you need help)
    `it alleges unlawful discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it alleges an act that is unlawful under Part 4 of the Age Discrimination Act (including victimisation), or an advertisement offence under s 50
    `it is reasonably arguable` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is reasonably arguable that what you allege is unlawful discrimination
    `I am aggrieved, or a person or union lodges it for me` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are a person aggrieved, or a person or trade union is lodging it on your behalf
    `I already complained or sued under a State or Territory law about the same act` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you have already made a complaint or started a proceeding about the same act under a State or Territory discrimination law (for example the WA Equal Opportunity Act 1984)

@export Can I lodge a complaint of age discrimination with the Australian Human Rights Commission (AHRC Act s 46P; ADA s 12(4))?
GIVEN `my complaint` IS A `My complaint` @desc Your complaint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I complain to the Commission` IF
        `my complaint`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `my complaint`'s `it alleges unlawful discrimination`
    AND `my complaint`'s `it is reasonably arguable`
    AND `my complaint`'s `I am aggrieved, or a person or union lodges it for me`
    AND (NOT `my complaint`'s `I already complained or sued under a State or Territory law about the same act`)

-- AHRC Act s 46PH(1): "The President may terminate a complaint on any of the following grounds: ... (b) the complaint was
-- lodged more than 24 months after the alleged acts, omissions or practices took place". A discretion, not a bar: the
-- answer is whether the President MAY end it on that ground.
@export Could my complaint be ended because I lodged it too late (AHRC Act s 46PH(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the act happened on` IS A DATE @desc The day the act you complain of took place
      `I lodge it on` IS A DATE @desc The day you lodge the complaint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the President end my complaint because it is late` IF
    `I lodge it on` GREATER THAN `add months` `the act happened on` 24

-- AHRC Act s 46PO(1), (2): once the President terminates the complaint and gives notice under s 46PH(2), an application
-- may be made to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); it "must be made
-- within 60 days after the date of issue of the notice under subsection 46PH(2), or within such further time as the court
-- concerned allows." The further time is the court's to allow: not encoded.
@export By when must I apply to the court after my complaint is terminated (AHRC Act s 46PO(2))?
GIVEN `the termination notice was issued on` IS A DATE @desc The date of issue of the President's notice terminating your complaint
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to the court` IS `the termination notice was issued on` PLUS 60
